# Copy to .env and fill in. Do not commit .env.
# Restart the dev server after changing anything here, Vite only reads it at startup.
#
# Every value in this file belongs in the browser bundle, and Firebase's own
# documentation says so: none of them is a secret. They name the project, they
# do not grant anything. What decides who may read and write what is
# db/firestore.rules, which runs on Google's side where nobody can edit it.
#
# The one real secret in this project is the service account key the seed
# script wants. That bypasses every rule, so it never goes here, never goes in
# the repository, and .gitignore already covers the usual names.
#
# Find the first four in the Firebase console under Project settings, General,
# in the "Your apps" section, after adding a Web app.
#
# Leave them empty and the app still runs: it serves the sample campus bundled
# in src/lib/campusRows.ts, View demo works, and the login screen says why
# signing in is unavailable. Set them in Vercel as well as here, or the
# deployed copy stays on the sample data.

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# App Check, which is what tells Firebase a request came from this app rather
# than from a script holding a copy of the four values above. Public like the
# rest of this file: a reCAPTCHA site key is read straight out of the page it
# runs on, and it is the rules that decide what a request may touch.
#
# Optional, and separate from the four above on purpose. Leave it empty and
# App Check never starts, which is the right outcome for anyone cloning this
# repository without a reCAPTCHA key of their own. The console makes one under
# Build, App Check, Apps, using the reCAPTCHA Enterprise provider.
#
# Set it in Vercel as well and redeploy. Vite reads this at build time and
# writes the value into the bundle, so adding it in Vercel on its own changes
# nothing until the next build. That is worth knowing before App Check
# enforcement is switched on, because from that moment a deployment built
# without this key is refused every single request, and a dashboard that can
# read nothing looks like a broken database rather than a missing variable.

VITE_FIREBASE_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=
